{
  "0": "Change only interaction scoring to diagonal bilinear compatibility: s(h,e)=sum_d [(1+0.5*tanh(a_d))*h_d*e_d], with jointly learned a initialized to zero. Apply this at the existing compatibility interface, preserving any surrounding score terms. Bounded dimension weights may suppress noisy interest coordinates without destabilizing initial scores. Preserve GRU topology, features, readout, loss and optimizer; update the predictor writer consistently.",
  "1": "Add a small residual bottleneck inside the recurrent network: transform each GRU output h to h+W_up(GELU(W_down(h))), using bottleneck width max(8, hidden_size/4) and zero-initialized W_up. Feed these outputs to the unchanged history readout. This preserves the initial GRU behavior while allowing nonlinear refinement at modest compute cost. Keep features, embeddings, scoring, loss and optimizer fixed, and mirror the architecture in the predictor writer.",
  "2": "Change only input feature construction: multiply each existing item input embedding by 1/sqrt(1+0.25*log(1+c)), where c counts earlier occurrences of that item in the available sequence prefix. Compute counts causally, exclude padding, and use the identical rule at inference. Mild repeat attenuation may prevent redundant interactions from dominating recurrent updates. Keep embedding parameters/design, GRU topology, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer unchanged.",
  "3": "Change only the existing pairwise softplus objective by adding a fixed positive margin of 0.2: softplus(0.2+s_negative-s_positive). Preserve existing loss weights, valid-position masks and reduction, with no new hard-negative weighting. Requiring additional positive-negative separation may improve top-10 ranking while retaining smooth gradients. Keep features, embeddings, GRU topology, scoring/readout, optimizer, sampling, scheduler and batch/epoch settings fixed."
